## Decision rule

Evidence for a shared digit/animal output workspace requires both:

- Digit–animal principal-angle overlap near the animal-space split-half noise ceiling and clearly above random.
- The animal-output basis recovers or removes numerical digit effects substantially better than random and comparably to the digit-read basis at matched rank.

Geometric overlap alone can arise from generic high-gain residual directions. Functional substitution is what shows that the overlapping directions actually carry the numerical effect.